------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Provenance
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The cryptographic core in `packages/sdk/` was originally written by the same
author inside the Cluster project (Oppia Software Labs) and is re-published here
under Apache-2.0. Only files authored solely by aguilar1x were carried over,
verified per-file against the source repository's git history. No third-party
contributor's code from that project is included.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Specifications implemented
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This project implements client obligations defined by OpenZeppelin's
Confidential Tokens specifications:

  - SDK.md
    https://github.com/OpenZeppelin/stellar-contracts/blob/main/packages/tokens/src/confidential/docs/SDK.md
  - INDEXER.md
    https://github.com/OpenZeppelin/stellar-contracts/blob/main/packages/tokens/src/confidential/docs/INDEXER.md

Those specifications are authored by OpenZeppelin and are not covered by this
project's copyright. This project is an independent implementation and is not
endorsed by or affiliated with OpenZeppelin.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Vendored material
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

`packages/conformance/fixtures/` — including its README.md — is a verbatim,
unmodified copy of OpenZeppelin's cross-language test vectors, taken from:

  https://github.com/OpenZeppelin/stellar-contracts/tree/main/packages/tokens/src/confidential/circuits/lib/testdata

They are vendored so the conformance suite runs offline and so the expected
values are OpenZeppelin's rather than this project's. Copyright OpenZeppelin,
Apache-2.0; not covered by this project's copyright.

`packages/conformance/scripts/check-fixtures-upstream.mjs` re-fetches every
fixture from that source and byte-compares it, on every push and on a weekly
schedule, so the vendored copy cannot silently diverge from upstream.

`circuits/lib/` — including its README.md — is a verbatim, unmodified copy of
OpenZeppelin's Noir circuit library, taken at commit 98090b3 from:

  https://github.com/OpenZeppelin/stellar-contracts/tree/98090b3e59785454f55b3617992c2f84250c7173/packages/tokens/src/confidential/circuits/lib

That is the commit the verifier deployed on testnet was built from. It is
vendored rather than fetched because Nargo can pin a git dependency to a branch
or tag name but never to a commit, and a branch pin would let this project's
circuits change meaning without a line of this project changing. Copyright
OpenZeppelin, Apache-2.0; not covered by this project's copyright.

`scripts/check-lib-upstream.mjs` re-fetches it at that exact commit and
byte-compares it on every push.

The circuits that USE that library — `circuits/disclose_sender/` and
`circuits/disclose_recipient/` — are this project's own work: OpenZeppelin
publishes a selective-disclosure specification, not an implementation.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party dependencies
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Proving is performed by Aztec's Barretenberg (`@aztec/bb.js`) and Noir
(`@noir-lang/noir_js`), and field/curve/hash primitives come from the Noble
libraries (`@noble/curves`, `@noble/hashes`, `@noble/ciphers`) and
`@zkpassport/poseidon2`. Each is distributed under its own license; see the
respective packages for details.
